---
/*
  Home.

  KOMPLETTER COPY-UMBAU 08.09.2026. Manuel hat die Fassung vom Morgen
  abgelehnt: zu viele Denkfehler in der Copy. Was hier geaendert wurde und
  warum, Punkt fuer Punkt:

  1. Headline. Die alte Zeile stellte das Wort "against" zwischen uns und die
     Creatorin. Zwei Fehler in einer Zeile. Erstens liest eine Frau, deren
     Englisch Fremdsprache ist, dort "gegen sie". Zweitens schaute die Zeile
     zurueck auf ihre alten Zahlen, statt nach vorn. Wer schon gut laeuft, dem
     verspricht der Satz nur, nicht schlechter zu sein als vorher.
     Neu: "You make the content. We do the rest." Sie ist die Handelnde, wir
     sind die Arbeit dahinter. Female-Gaze-Dossier Abschnitt 4.
  2. Subheadline. Keine Umsatzversprechen, keine Zahl als Versprechen. Sie
     benennt nur, was wir tun, und was sie davon hat: ihre Woche.
     Nachgeschaerft am 08.09.2026 nach dem Zielgruppen-Rat, Protokoll
     projects/zielgruppen-rat/protokolle/2026-09-08-0924-wunder-hero-v3-*.md:
     Die erste Fassung endete auf "your page can grow, and you can earn more".
     Alle sieben Stimmen haben genau diese Zeile als "wieder so eine Agentur"
     markiert, Vertrauensschnitt 3.2 bei Kaufhandlung 3.0. Ein Versprechen
     ohne Grenze wirkt in dieser Zielgruppe gegen den Absender. Die Zeile ist
     ersetzt durch die drei Zusicherungen, die vier von fuenf Kernpersonas
     unabhaengig voneinander vermisst haben: Geld zuerst bei ihr, nichts geht
     ohne ihr Ja raus, sie kann aufhoeren. Dahinter der Verweis auf die
     Beweisseite statt auf eine Moeglichkeit.
  3. Der Abschnitt "You know what your account did at its best" ist raus. Er
     widersprach dem eigenen Mechanismus: die Grundlinie sind die letzten
     dreissig Tage, nicht der beste Monat. Der Mechanismus steht weiter auf
     /how-it-works, dort gehoert er hin.
  4. Der Name der Fan-Plattform steht nirgends mehr. Grund: Banken.
  5. Keine Toolnamen mehr. Ersatz: "the programs we built for
     this".
  6. Passwort. Der Abschnitt behauptete "You never hand us a password". Das ist
     falsch. Korrektur Manuel 08.09.2026: die Creatorin gibt uns das Passwort,
     damit sich unsere Programme verbinden koennen. Ein Mensch loggt sich nie
     direkt ein.
  7. "How you get paid" bleibt und ist kuerzer: keine Setup-Gebuehr, kein
     Mindestumsatz, das Geld geht direkt auf ihr Konto, wir stellen danach
     unsere Rechnung, einmal die Woche.
  8. Jeder Abschnitt hat jetzt ein Bild, abwechselnd links und rechts. Vorher
     stand ausser im Kopf nirgends eines. Regel Manuel: nie Text auf Text.

  BINDEND, gilt weiter:
  Kein Revenue Split auf der Seite (Manuel 07.09. abends, bestaetigt 08.09.).
  Keine Laufzeit, keine Kuendigungsfrist, keine Verlaengerung.
  Jeder Satz kurz und einfach, siehe scripts/check-copy.mjs, Regeln 5 bis 8.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import Split from '../components/Split.astro';
import { legal } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Wunder | You make the content, we do the rest"
  description="Wunder works with creators. We plan your posts, we write to your fans and we sell for you. Your money reaches your bank first, and you see every step in your own portal."
>
  <Split
    image="creator-speaking.webp"
    alt="A creator sits at a microphone and talks. She uses her hands while she explains something."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="A creator we work with, talking about her own month."
    eager
  >
    <h1>You make the content. We do the rest.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      We work with creators like you. We plan your posts. We write to your fans. We sell for you.
      You get your week back.
    </p>
    <ul class="promise">
      <li>Your money reaches your bank first.</li>
      <li>Nothing goes out in your name without your yes.</li>
      <li>You can leave when the work no longer suits you.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Want to see where that got other creators? <a href="/results">Look at their own screens</a>.
    </p>
    <CtaBlock secondary />
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="creator-and-manager-table.webp"
    alt="A creator and Lauris sit at the same table and talk. Both are at the same height in the picture."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="We sit down with every creator before anything starts."
    flip
  >
    <h2>What do you need help with?</h2>
    <p class="lead">Most creators come to us for one of four things.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>More fans, because growth has stopped.</li>
      <li>Help with the daily work that is not the content.</li>
      <li>A plan for what to post, and when.</li>
      <li>Free time. Some of them just want their week back.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>What matters most to you? Tell us on the call.</p>
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="case-followers.webp"
    alt="A follower report for one account. The number of new follows in the period is three hundred twenty four thousand."
    width={1300}
    height={1016}
    caption="One account. New followers over five months. This is her own report."
  >
    <h2>We show you, we do not tell you.</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Any agency can promise you a big month. We would rather put the screen next to the words.
    </p>
    <p>
      On our results page you see what happened on real accounts. What they earned. How their
      followers grew. And what those creators wrote about us in their own words.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/results">See the results</a></p>
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="portal-login-desktop.webp"
    alt="The portal login screen on a laptop, with fields for email and password."
    width={1200}
    height={750}
    caption="Your own login. You do not need to ask us for numbers."
    flip
  >
    <h2>You see the same screen we do.</h2>
    <p>
      Every post goes through our own portal. We read each number where it comes from. We do not
      guess it.
    </p>
    <p>
      You log into your own portal. There you see views, reach and followers. You can look at
      seven, thirty and ninety days. You see the plan your manager wrote.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/how-it-works#portal">See how it works</a></p>
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="portal-login-mobile.webp"
    alt="The same login screen on a phone."
    width={430}
    height={932}
    caption="One login for you. Our programs use their own."
    narrow
  >
    <h2>What happens with your password.</h2>
    <p>
      You give us the password for your page. Our programs need it so they can connect. That is the
      only reason we ask for it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nobody here opens your account by hand. All the work runs through the programs we built for
      this. So there is a record of what was done, and when.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/how-it-works#access">See how it works</a></p>
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="lauris-speaking.webp"
    alt="Lauris sits at a microphone and explains something. He is looking at the person across the table."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="Lauris runs the day to day work with the team."
    flip
  >
    <h2>We check the people who write to your fans.</h2>
    <p>
      Someone writes to your fans in your name. That is the one thing we do as you. So we read that
      work back, and never by the person who wrote it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Twice a week our system takes the last finished shift and scores it against written rules.
      Nobody on the chat team can switch that check off.
    </p>
    <p>
      Chatters are people. Now and then a message comes out wrong. When that happens we tell you,
      and we put it right with you.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/how-it-works#chatting">See how it works</a></p>
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="creator-checkin.webp"
    alt="A creator and Lauris sit at a podcast table with a Wunder sign behind them."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="We go through the money on the call, not on a web page."
  >
    <h2>How you get paid.</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There is no setup fee.</li>
      <li>There is no minimum you have to earn.</li>
      <li>The money goes straight to your bank.</li>
      <li>We send our bill after that, once a week.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We go through the numbers on the call. You sign nothing before that. You can leave early if
      the work no longer suits you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your content stays yours. When you go, we switch your portal access off the same day.
    </p>
    <CtaBlock />
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="founders-call.webp"
    alt="Manuel and Lauris talk to each other on a video call, each in his own room."
    width={324}
    height={360}
    caption="Manuel and Lauris. They run the company together."
    flip
    narrow
  >
    <h2>A real company, with two people who sign for it.</h2>
    <p>
      Wunder is a brand by {legal.company}. The number in the register is {legal.regNumber}. The
      company started in Riga on {legal.registered}.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two directors run it, and each one may sign alone. Manuel Gonzalez is CEO and co owner.
      Lauris Kalnins is COO and co owner.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can look all of that up first. <a href="/company">The company page has the rest</a>.
    </p>
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="creator-meeting-blue.webp"
    alt="A creator and Lauris sit across from each other and talk in a studio with blue light."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="Every creator we work with started with one short form."
  >
    <h2>Apply, and we tell you either way.</h2>
    <p>
      You send eight short answers. A person reads them. Then you hear if it is a fit. If it is not,
      you get one line that says so. You get an answer, not silence.
    </p>
    <CtaBlock secondary />
  </Split>
</Base>
